00:36:00.470 --> 00:36:02.129
And over those 20 years, we've

00:36:02.130 --> 00:36:03.269
developed a tremendous amount of

00:36:03.270 --> 00:36:04.089
intelligence.

00:36:04.090 --> 00:36:06.029
Best practice processes, rules

00:36:06.030 --> 00:36:08.169
engines, and with

00:36:08.170 --> 00:36:10.289
the AI revolution that's happening,

00:36:10.290 --> 00:36:11.529
at the beginning of this year, we

00:36:11.530 --> 00:36:12.749
decided we needed to take a

00:36:12.750 --> 00:36:13.969
fundamentally different approach,

00:36:13.970 --> 00:36:15.149
and we've been embedding that

00:36:15.150 --> 00:36:17.209
intelligence in what we call a

00:36:17.210 --> 00:36:19.569
revenue operating system.

00:36:19.570 --> 00:36:21.329
We call it Fair OS.

00:36:21.330 --> 00:36:23.149
The revenue operating system is

00:36:23.150 --> 00:36:25.329
aimed at comprehensively automating

00:36:25.330 --> 00:36:27.389
complex processes to accelerate

00:36:27.390 --> 00:36:29.289
reimbursement and to make it as

00:36:29.290 --> 00:36:30.809
accurate as possible.

00:36:30.810 --> 00:36:31.849
And importantly, it's an

00:36:31.850 --> 00:36:33.709
interconnected system that is aimed

00:36:33.710 --> 00:36:35.609
not just at resolving problems but

00:36:35.610 --> 00:36:36.869
preventing them in the first place.

00:36:43.470 --> 00:36:44.470
Oh, OK.

00:36:45.950 --> 00:36:48.169
So denials represent a

00:36:48.170 --> 00:36:49.649
huge administrative burden in health

00:36:49.650 --> 00:36:50.669
care.

00:36:50.670 --> 00:36:52.709
We know at R1 that 9%

00:36:52.710 --> 00:36:54.809
of claims will be

00:36:54.810 --> 00:36:56.889
first pass denied.

00:36:56.890 --> 00:36:58.689
After weeks of administrative back

00:36:58.690 --> 00:37:01.190
and forth, phone calls,

00:37:02.490 --> 00:37:04.749
gathering evidence, clinicians going

00:37:04.750 --> 00:37:06.209
back and fourth, you'll end up with

00:37:06.210 --> 00:37:08.169
only a small fraction will actually

00:37:08.170 --> 00:37:09.170
stay denied.

00:37:09.890 --> 00:37:11.129
And so to address that

00:37:11.130 --> 00:37:12.839
administrative burden, We've built

00:37:12.840 --> 00:37:14.659
the Fair OS, Revenue Cycle

00:37:14.660 --> 00:37:15.819
Operating System.

00:37:15.820 --> 00:37:16.960
It's completely agentic.

00:37:18.380 --> 00:37:20.199
The system starts with the

00:37:20.200 --> 00:37:22.239
triage and orchestration agent that

00:37:22.240 --> 00:37:24.839
takes in all the data that

00:37:24.840 --> 00:37:26.759
a payer provides, the clinical

00:37:26.760 --> 00:37:28.579
records, combine it, and

00:37:28.580 --> 00:37:30.619
routes any

00:37:30.620 --> 00:37:32.559
potential denial to a specialized

00:37:32.560 --> 00:37:34.499
agent that knows how to address

00:37:34.500 --> 00:37:36.139
and solve that problem.

00:37:36.140 --> 00:37:38.259
Could be

00:37:38.260 --> 00:37:40.259
an eligibility auth denial,

00:37:40.260 --> 00:37:41.419
and that agent.

00:37:41.420 --> 00:37:42.819
Is the specialist that knows how to

00:37:42.820 --> 00:37:44.259
go through and solve it.

00:37:44.260 --> 00:37:46.279
Let's look at an example of a

00:37:46.280 --> 00:37:48.040
completed denial that was processed.

00:37:52.000 --> 00:37:53.579
Here's the complete account where

00:37:53.580 --> 00:37:54.939
the pair requested additional

00:37:54.940 --> 00:37:55.999
information.

00:37:56.000 --> 00:37:57.399
The triage agent received

00:37:57.400 --> 00:37:59.359
information and routed to

00:37:59.360 --> 00:38:01.519
specialized, lax information.

00:38:01.520 --> 00:38:03.379
The agent got to work, reading the

00:38:03.380 --> 00:38:04.979
medical record, looking at the

00:38:04.980 --> 00:38:07.129
denial which explained

00:38:07.130 --> 00:38:08.919
what information was needed, looking

00:38:08.920 --> 00:38:10.839
through the ontology and identifying

00:38:10.840 --> 00:38:13.559
all the information the pair needs.

00:38:13.560 --> 00:38:15.179
The agent then gathered the required

00:38:15.180 --> 00:38:16.779
documentation together into a

00:38:16.780 --> 00:38:18.679
cohesive packet ready to send

00:38:18.680 --> 00:38:20.279
and actually sent it to the pair.

00:38:20.280 --> 00:38:21.989
Automatically.

00:38:21.990 --> 00:38:23.869
Completely automatically.

00:38:23.870 --> 00:38:25.229
In this case, this is completely

00:38:25.230 --> 00:38:27.229
resolved without human intervention

00:38:27.230 --> 00:38:28.689
at all.

00:38:28.690 --> 00:38:29.629
This is a process that would

00:38:29.630 --> 00:38:31.209
typically take about 20 to 40

00:38:31.210 --> 00:38:32.629
minutes for a person to just look

00:38:32.630 --> 00:38:33.629
through everything, try to

00:38:33.630 --> 00:38:35.109
understand what's going on, and

00:38:35.110 --> 00:38:36.089
collect the packet and send it

00:38:36.090 --> 00:38:37.249
through.

00:38:37.250 --> 00:38:39.009
This agent orchestration.

00:38:39.010 --> 00:38:40.669
The right agent working on the right

00:38:40.670 --> 00:38:41.670
problem at the right time.

00:38:44.660 --> 00:38:46.039
Next, let's take a look at an

00:38:46.040 --> 00:38:47.659
in-progress case requiring an

00:38:47.660 --> 00:38:48.579
appeal.

00:38:48.580 --> 00:38:49.919
In this case, the triage agent

00:38:49.920 --> 00:38:51.919
identified the

00:38:51.920 --> 00:38:53.599
denial and routed it to an appeals

00:38:53.600 --> 00:38:55.699
agent, which gathers clinical

00:38:55.700 --> 00:38:57.679
documentation, research the

00:38:57.680 --> 00:38:59.519
payer's denial rationale, and

00:38:59.520 --> 00:39:00.520
drafts an appeal letter.

00:39:01.980 --> 00:39:03.559
Here's where human-AI collaboration

00:39:03.560 --> 00:39:05.099
becomes critical.

00:39:05.100 --> 00:39:07.319
Appeals require clinical judgment,

00:39:07.320 --> 00:39:08.979
so the agent surfaces a

00:39:08.980 --> 00:39:10.759
recommendation for a specialist to

00:39:10.760 --> 00:39:11.719
review and refine.

00:39:11.720 --> 00:39:13.699
It's not replacing humans,

00:39:13.700 --> 00:39:14.949
it empowers them.

00:39:14.950 --> 00:39:16.889
The agent handles the tedious work

00:39:16.890 --> 00:39:18.989
of gathering all this data so

00:39:18.990 --> 00:39:20.189
the specialist can focus on the

00:39:20.190 --> 00:39:21.190
high-value decision.

00:39:22.030 --> 00:39:23.209
It's a model we believe translates

00:39:23.210 --> 00:39:24.809
across industries.

00:39:24.810 --> 00:39:26.029
AI handles volumes and the

00:39:26.030 --> 00:39:27.829
complexity of big data, and humans

00:39:27.830 --> 00:39:29.389
provide judgment and expertise.

00:39:30.470 --> 00:39:32.149
Zooming out, these are all examples

00:39:32.150 --> 00:39:34.469
of just one workflow each,

00:39:34.470 --> 00:39:36.009
but behind this is a system of

00:39:36.010 --> 00:39:37.489
agents that constantly are working

00:39:37.490 --> 00:39:39.489
in parallel across thousands of

00:39:39.490 --> 00:39:41.389
accounts, each managed by an

00:39:41.390 --> 00:39:42.849
appropriate agent, with human

00:39:42.850 --> 00:39:44.190
oversight where it matters most.

00:39:45.730 --> 00:39:47.589
What makes this all possible is the

00:39:47.590 --> 00:39:49.769
unified ontology connecting clinical

00:39:49.770 --> 00:39:51.689
data, claims data, payer

00:39:51.690 --> 00:39:53.429
rules and appeals history together

00:39:53.430 --> 00:39:54.949
along with the final outcome.

00:39:56.010 --> 00:39:57.889
So an agent's handoff work, they

00:39:57.890 --> 00:39:59.389
pass the full context.

00:39:59.390 --> 00:40:01.089
The triage agent makes sure the lax

00:40:01.090 --> 00:40:02.409
info agent sees what's been tried

00:40:02.410 --> 00:40:04.349
before, what documentation

00:40:04.350 --> 00:40:06.009
was submitted and what the payer

00:40:06.010 --> 00:40:07.529
requires.

00:40:07.530 --> 00:40:09.109
And critically, every decision,

00:40:09.110 --> 00:40:11.249
every action that got taken by

00:40:11.250 --> 00:40:13.189
humans and AI

00:40:13.190 --> 00:40:14.529
and all the decision and final

00:40:14.530 --> 00:40:15.749
outcome makes it back to the

00:40:15.750 --> 00:40:16.829
ontology.

00:40:16.830 --> 00:40:19.309
So our agents get smarter over time.

00:40:19.310 --> 00:40:20.709
