00:50:02.620 --> 00:50:04.199
construction company to have true

00:50:04.200 --> 00:50:05.839
operational AI.

00:50:05.840 --> 00:50:07.359
We didn't just bring Foundry into

00:50:07.360 --> 00:50:09.359
our business, we put our business

00:50:09.360 --> 00:50:11.119
in Foundry, and we're gonna prove

00:50:11.120 --> 00:50:12.239
that you can run your business with

00:50:12.240 --> 00:50:13.240
nothing but.

00:50:14.300 --> 00:50:15.979
We're planning for the long term.

00:50:15.980 --> 00:50:17.119
We're excited to announce that we're

00:50:17.120 --> 00:50:17.999
partnering with Palantir to

00:50:18.000 --> 00:50:19.579
commercialize these solutions across

00:50:19.580 --> 00:50:20.979
the industry.

00:50:20.980 --> 00:50:22.659
Together with Palatir, we're raising

00:50:22.660 --> 00:50:24.279
the ceiling for construction and

00:50:24.280 --> 00:50:25.280
with it the floor.

00:50:25.980 --> 00:50:27.879
The fastest route to operational AI

00:50:27.880 --> 00:50:30.279
is to run your business through it.

00:50:30.280 --> 00:50:31.799
Go all in.

00:50:31.800 --> 00:50:32.800
Thank you so much for your time.

00:50:37.310 --> 00:50:38.949
Please welcome Head of Corporate

00:50:38.950 --> 00:50:40.809
Development at Palantir,

00:50:40.810 --> 00:50:41.810
Sasha Spivak.

00:50:49.830 --> 00:50:51.709
Another round of applause for our

00:50:51.710 --> 00:50:52.710
speakers.

00:50:58.510 --> 00:51:00.549
I wanna talk a little bit about one

00:51:00.550 --> 00:51:02.329
of the biggest things I've learned

00:51:02.330 --> 00:51:04.309
at Palantir over the last 10

00:51:04.310 --> 00:51:07.209
years, which is trust.

00:51:07.210 --> 00:51:08.549
I have a mechanical engineering

00:51:08.550 --> 00:51:10.429
background and was hired as a

00:51:10.430 --> 00:51:12.729
writer, a job I was absolutely

00:51:12.730 --> 00:51:14.069
unqualified for.

00:51:14.070 --> 00:51:15.689
In fact, in my hiring thesis, it

00:51:15.690 --> 00:51:17.130
quite literally said weaknesses.

00:51:19.700 --> 00:51:21.739
When I landed and was doing

00:51:21.740 --> 00:51:23.139
the job that I was obviously never

00:51:23.140 --> 00:51:25.019
going to be good at,

00:51:25.020 --> 00:51:26.899
I got my first dose of what

00:51:26.900 --> 00:51:28.719
it means to trust.

00:51:28.720 --> 00:51:30.739
I had to trust that the

00:51:30.740 --> 00:51:32.419
team, and specifically the person

00:51:32.420 --> 00:51:34.299
who took a bet on me, saw

00:51:34.300 --> 00:51:36.179
something. I had trust that they

00:51:36.180 --> 00:51:38.340
believed that I would see something.

00:51:39.780 --> 00:51:41.519
Many years later, when we were going

00:51:41.520 --> 00:51:43.519
public, and I took a moment

00:51:43.520 --> 00:51:45.439
to reflect on the

00:51:45.440 --> 00:51:47.239
gravity of the thing that I got to

00:51:47.240 --> 00:51:48.469
be working on, and the.

00:51:48.470 --> 00:51:50.469
People that I was doing that

00:51:50.470 --> 00:51:51.809
with.

00:51:51.810 --> 00:51:53.529
And I had another realization.

00:51:53.530 --> 00:51:55.469
I said, excuse my language,

00:51:55.470 --> 00:51:57.509
who fucked up and trusted me

00:51:57.510 --> 00:51:59.349
with what I'm currently doing and

00:51:59.350 --> 00:52:00.710
who I'm doing it with?

00:52:01.890 --> 00:52:03.189
And that was sort of my second

00:52:03.190 --> 00:52:04.269
lesson in trust.

00:52:04.270 --> 00:52:06.049
It was like no one fucked up.

00:52:06.050 --> 00:52:08.089
They trusted me, and so I had

00:52:08.090 --> 00:52:09.090
to trust them.

00:52:11.510 --> 00:52:13.309
And then later came a third form of

00:52:13.310 --> 00:52:15.469
trust, the kind where

00:52:15.470 --> 00:52:17.409
Alex frequently has these ideas

00:52:17.410 --> 00:52:19.749
where you just have to believe

00:52:19.750 --> 00:52:21.749
until you see that they come true

00:52:21.750 --> 00:52:23.769
every single time, like his most

00:52:23.770 --> 00:52:25.749
recent one, which was we have

00:52:25.750 --> 00:52:27.709
to hire kids out of high school who

00:52:27.710 --> 00:52:29.669
when they look at a college campus,

00:52:29.670 --> 00:52:31.429
see a woke education, an unsafe

00:52:31.430 --> 00:52:33.369
place to be, and you

00:52:33.370 --> 00:52:34.370
just to have to.

00:52:36.420 --> 00:52:38.019
And instead of just going with it,

00:52:38.020 --> 00:52:39.799
you have to commit to it until you

00:52:39.800 --> 00:52:41.359
manifest that reality into

00:52:41.360 --> 00:52:42.360
existence.

00:52:43.300 --> 00:52:45.399
And today, I'm

00:52:45.400 --> 00:52:47.219
reminded of the fourth form

00:52:47.220 --> 00:52:48.859
of trust, which is being with all of

00:52:48.860 --> 00:52:50.359
you in this room. And that's the

00:52:50.360 --> 00:52:51.460
trust of being with family.

00:52:53.080 --> 00:52:55.279
We ask you to trust us

00:52:55.280 --> 00:52:57.559
with really unbearably high

00:52:57.560 --> 00:52:58.560
missions.

00:52:59.780 --> 00:53:01.659
And we trust you with

00:53:01.660 --> 00:53:02.660
those as well.

00:53:03.360 --> 00:53:05.479
I feel very grateful, very humbled,

00:53:05.480 --> 00:53:07.819
very proud to be in a room with

00:53:07.820 --> 00:53:09.919
people that we trust

00:53:11.020 --> 00:53:12.959
implicitly and it is incredible to

00:53:12.960 --> 00:53:14.119
be trusted with the same thing.

